      "side": 1,
      "message": "When you reference a method from a class object you get a method that isn\u0027t bound to a particular instance so there is no magic \u0027self\u0027. You can call it, but you have to pass in the instance manually like: C.m(C())\n\nIf you reference the method from an instance then you get a method that effectively curries the self argument for you (think functools.partial).",
